    // "tools" here is load-bearing for context size, not just permissions: measured
    // 2026-08-15, excluding desktop-touch_* drops this agent's baseline from 163,136
    // to 130,933 tokens (-32,203, i.e. 20% of the whole context). The tool schemas are
    // genuinely removed from the prompt, not merely blocked at call time. desktop-touch
    // is a second GUI-automation stack that no agent actually references -- pc-operator,
    // the desktop agent, drives open-controller/windows-mcp instead -- so nothing loses
    // a capability here. Re-enable by deleting the "tools" key, or move it to a subagent
    // that needs it: subagents pay for their own tools only while they run.
    // github_* moved off the orchestrator 2026-08-15 (23 tools, 2,967 tokens by the real
    // tokenizer). The capability is unchanged -- git-agent still resolves all 23 as true,
    // verified with `opencode debug agent git-agent`: a deny here does NOT cascade to
    // subagents. Reach them by delegating to git-agent.
    //
    // Written as `permission` and not `tools` on purpose. Both were tested and both flip
    // the resolved tool map identically (23/23 false), but `tools` is deprecated in the
    // docs in favour of `permission`, and issue anomalyco/opencode#37675 reports the
    // GLOBAL `tools` key failing to exclude MCP tools from provider requests. Per-agent
    // is a different code path and works, but there is no reason to build on the
    // deprecated field when the supported one produces the same state.
    // assistant (2026-08-27): foi DEFAULT durante 2 dias para poupar o GLM 5.3 do
    // `orchestrator` em conversa avulsa. REVERTIDO 2026-08-29: default_agent voltou a
    // `orchestrator` (ver topo do ficheiro). O `assistant` mantem-se como fallback
    // rapido read-only (smart-free), acessivel por troca manual de agente.
    "assistant": {
      "model": "smart-router/smart-free",
      "mode": "subagent",
      "prompt": "Fast fallback for trivial read-only lookups. The primary session runs on the `orchestrator`; delegate any mutation to `coder`."
    },
    "orchestrator": {
      "mode": "primary",
      // 2026-09-04: steps cap added after ses_f96b45f0cffedj1m4dihINdUlH
      // post-mortem. Noites sessions can run unbounded iterations otherwise.
      // 200 covers ~20h budget at 1 iter/6min average; subagent delegation
      // makes this a soft ceiling not a hard limit (subagents count their own
      // steps). Set lower (50) for daily sessions if context gets tight.
      "steps": 200,
      "tools": {
        "desktop-touch_*": false
      },
      "model": "smart-router/smart-orchestrator",
      "permission": {
        // Denied 2026-08-15 from measured evidence, not guesswork. Each of these
        // tools has ZERO invocations across all 404 sessions in opencode.db, while
        // costing schema tokens in every single request. Costs come from magic
        // context's tool_definition_measurements (real tokenizer at the provider
